triage: revise_rules: The game is built correctly, but a mindless policy (always the first option, which amounts to small lots and minimum bids) wins about 80-86% of decided games, and always taking the last option (bidding all your florins) always loses. Prizes are large and bids are cheap, so grabbing cards for 1 florin beats any thinking. Seat 2 also wins far more often than the other seats.
